# Leave // Chance, a split card (CR 709), pictured from both sides at once: Bot2 has just cast one as Leave, which waits
# on the stack, and Bot1 - the seat handed over - holds another and may answer with it.
#
# What the client has to draw: in hand, the whole card as it is printed (CR 709.1) - its two halves side by side along
# its length, each with its own name, cost, art and text, turned a quarter turn so the card reads turned clockwise, and
# held up turned that way. On the stack, only the half that was cast, as a whole card of its own (CR 709.3a): Leave,
# white, {1}{W}, and nothing of Chance.
#
# Bot2 casts it, not Bot1: a client passes its own priority after casting unless it is holding priority, so a spell of
# the handed-over seat's would be resolved before the page is looked at.

